WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.149 --> 00:00:04.310
There may not be a ton of blockbusters or
superhero flicks on tap for February, but

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:07.961
there are still more than enough great movies
to keep you busy at your local theater. From

00:00:07.961 --> 00:00:12.949
future award season fodder to animated comedies,
and a few mid-tier franchise sequels, here

00:00:12.949 --> 00:00:17.910
are all the movies worth checking out on the
big screen in February 2017.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:18.910
Rings

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:23.650
It's been about a decade since that wet weirdo
climbed out of a TV and killed a bunch of

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:27.699
people, and in the years since, that freaky
VHS tape is looking to make the transition

00:00:27.699 --> 00:00:32.520
into the digital age. The long-awaited sequel,
Rings, comes out on February 3rd, and picks

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.900
up about 13 years after the first film. It
follows a woman and her boyfriend who get

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:41.480
roped into the freaky drama of the horrific
tape, and it also aims to deepen the mythology

00:00:41.480 --> 00:00:46.830
with a secret message hidden inside the tape
that no one has found...until now.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:53.370
"The second it's over, the phone rings, and
this voice says…"

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.870
"...seven days."

00:00:54.870 --> 00:01:00.320
The film also features the tagline "First
you watch it. Then you die." So… good luck

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:01.650
with that.

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:03.940
The Space Between Us

00:01:03.940 --> 00:01:08.710
There are star-crossed lovers, and then there's
The Space Between Us, coming out on February

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:14.420
3rd. This fascinating teen love story follows
a boy born on Mars and the Earth girl he falls

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:19.350
in love with. Sixteen-year-old Gardner lives
his entire life with only the 14 other people

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:23.840
on the Red Planet, but finally gets a chance
to visit Earth and connect with his pen pal

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:28.710
Tulsa. Of course, his visit doesn't go as
planned when he realizes his body can't handle

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:33.600
Earth's atmosphere, and he embarks on a whirlwind
journey to try and figure out where he belongs

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.840
in life, and in the solar system.

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.950
John Wick: Chapter 2

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:44.549
2014's surprise hit John Wick proved the Keanu
Reeves was still able to kick butt, and expectations

00:01:44.549 --> 00:01:48.530
are high that John Wick: Chapter 2 can carry
on the trend when it comes out on February

00:01:48.530 --> 00:01:52.450
10th. The story follows Reeves' hitman as
he's pulled out of retirement to help a former

00:01:52.450 --> 00:01:56.920
associate take over an assassins' guild. The
supporting cast includes Common, Laurence

00:01:56.920 --> 00:02:01.909
Fishburne, Riccardo Scamarcio, Ruby Rose,
John Leguizamo, and Ian McShane, and the end

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:04.590
result promises to be a bloody, gritty thrill
ride.

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:06.190
"I'll kill them all."

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:07.790
"Of course you will."

00:02:07.790 --> 00:02:12.799
If this one works out, the studio is already
eyeballing a third film in the franchise.

00:02:12.799 --> 00:02:13.889
The LEGO Batman Movie

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:17.480
"Just go ahead when you're ready."

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:21.220
"Sorry I wasn't listening. I've just been Bat-mailing
on my Batphone."

00:02:21.230 --> 00:02:23.220
"Yeah, can you just do the line?"

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:26.959
Will Arnett's version of the Dark Knight was
a breakout performance in The LEGO Movie,

00:02:26.959 --> 00:02:30.790
so Warner Brothers decided to spin him off
into his own adventure. The early trailers

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:35.849
have looked outrageously funny, and the family-friendly
CGI tale promises to roll in a ton of players

00:02:35.849 --> 00:02:40.120
from across the Batman and DC universe to
tell what could be one of the best Batman

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:44.640
stories in years. If nothing else, it'll be
unlike pretty much every other DC movie on

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:45.640
the market.

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:46.640
"Superman is my greatest enemy."

00:02:46.640 --> 00:02:47.640
"Superman's not a bad guy."

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:55.590
"Then I'd say that I currently don't have
a bad guy. I am fighting a few different people.

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.510
I like to fight around."

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:01.450
If you're looking for a break from Zack Snyder's
grim world, this should do it. Prepare for

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:04.489
everything to be awesome again on February
10th.

00:03:04.489 --> 00:03:05.489
Fifty Shades Darker

00:03:05.489 --> 00:03:10.930
The second film in the Fifty Shades of Grey
saga arrives on February 10th, with stars

00:03:10.930 --> 00:03:15.769
Dakota Johnson and Jamie Dornan joined by
Kim Basinger, Tyler Hoechlin, and Hugh Dancy.

00:03:15.769 --> 00:03:19.549
The sequel picks up with Ana trying to move
past her relationship with Christian, but

00:03:19.549 --> 00:03:22.749
since this franchise is far from over, you
can probably guess they get back together

00:03:22.749 --> 00:03:27.269
— but this time under Ana's conditions.
The critically-panned original made a whole

00:03:27.269 --> 00:03:31.040
lot of money, so it'll be interesting to see
what new director James Foley brings to E.L.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:36.540
James' bondage tale. Don't bring your mom.
Or do, if you're weird.

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.430
The Great Wall

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:42.599
This fantasy action flick promises to be one
of the biggest Chinese film productions in

00:03:42.599 --> 00:03:47.500
history, attracting A-list Hollywood talent,
including Matt Damon, Willem Dafoe, and Pedro

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:52.139
Pascal. It's a period adventure about heroes
fighting off giant monsters during the Song

00:03:52.139 --> 00:03:57.760
dynasty, so historical accuracy doesn't really
figure anywhere into this. Releasing on February

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:02.190
17th, early footage from the film looks like
a white-knuckle thrill ride with a whole lot

00:04:02.190 --> 00:04:06.939
of monster-slaying action; Damon seems to
be channeling his Jason Bourne persona a bit,

00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:11.019
but hey, who wouldn't want to see Jason Bourne
slug it out with a giant monster?

00:04:11.019 --> 00:04:12.699
Fist Fight

00:04:12.699 --> 00:04:17.400
If you're a fan of HBO's cult hit Vice Principals,
this should be right up your alley. This Ice

00:04:17.400 --> 00:04:20.889
Cube vehicle features the Ride Along star
pitted against It's Always Sunny in Philadelphia's

00:04:20.889 --> 00:04:25.990
Charlie Day, as two teachers who are headed
towards an old-fashioned parking lot brawl

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.060
after one accidentally gets the other fired.

00:04:28.060 --> 00:04:31.610
"Parking lot, after school. It's on!"

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:34.810
Day is hilarious in pretty much anything,
and the early trailers look like he'll be

00:04:34.810 --> 00:04:39.210
an excellent foil for Ice Cube's style of
humor. Cut class to see this one on February

00:04:39.210 --> 00:04:40.470
17th.

00:04:40.470 --> 00:04:42.289
A Cure for Wellness

00:04:42.289 --> 00:04:46.970
This psychological horror thriller from acclaimed
director Gore Verbinski stars Dane DeHaan,

00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:51.479
Mia Goth, and Jason Isaacs. The story is about
a young executive sent to retrieve his company's

00:04:51.479 --> 00:04:56.360
CEO at a "wellness center" where it turns
out the spa's healing techniques are a bit

00:04:56.360 --> 00:05:00.320
too good to be true. Before long, he comes
down with a mystery illness that everyone

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:04.460
at the spa wants to cure. It looks to be a
twisty and terrifying tale, and it comes out

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:06.750
on February 17th.

00:05:06.750 --> 00:05:07.919
Get Out

00:05:07.919 --> 00:05:12.139
This racially charged horror film, scheduled
for February 24th, was written and directed

00:05:12.139 --> 00:05:16.550
by comedian Jordan Peele, who's described
the project as "a horror movie, [with] a satirical

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:21.220
premise." The story follows a young African-American
man who visits the family and estate of his

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:25.189
white girlfriend. When many of the black people
in the area start to vanish, the young man

00:05:25.189 --> 00:05:29.509
realizes this weekend visit is a lot more
dangerous than just meeting the parents. Peele

00:05:29.509 --> 00:05:33.919
is no stranger to racially-charged comedy-horror,
but this one seems a lot less funny than his

00:05:33.919 --> 00:05:34.919
previous efforts.

00:05:36.680 --> 00:05:37.911
"Ain't that some s***."

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:41.100
"These are some racist, mother f***in' zombies."

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:48.340
"Why would you even lock the door, I mean
the window is broken… oh hell no!"

00:05:48.340 --> 00:05:50.150
Rock Dog

00:05:50.150 --> 00:05:55.060
This CGI tale of a dog from a small town looking
to make it as a rock star has turned out to

00:05:55.060 --> 00:06:00.139
be a box office dud in its native China, but
there's hope U.S. audiences will come out

00:06:00.139 --> 00:06:04.949
to see Luke Wilson's anthropomorphic mutt
chase his dream of being a rock star on February

00:06:04.949 --> 00:06:09.460
24th. If trying to make it in music wasn't
hard enough, Wilson's pup will also have to

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:13.610
contend with a rogue wolf pack. Along with
Wilson, the film also features the voices

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:18.979
of Eddie Izzard, J. K. Simmons, Lewis Black,
Kenan Thompson, Mae Whitman, Jorge Garcia,

00:06:18.979 --> 00:06:20.610
and Matt Dillon.

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:21.610
Collide

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:26.219
Kicking around development since 2013, Collide
will makes its American debut on February

00:06:26.219 --> 00:06:32.159
24th, 2017, after its German release in 2016.
The story tracks a heist gone wrong, leaving

00:06:32.159 --> 00:06:36.580
a young man on the run from a dangerous mob
boss, played by the imposing Anthony Hopkins.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:41.699
He then turns to his old drug-smuggling employer,
played by Ben Kingsley, for help. All the

00:06:41.699 --> 00:06:45.551
while, he tries to protect his girlfriend,
played by Rogue One's Felicity Jones. With

00:06:45.551 --> 00:06:49.500
Jones' star on the rise, it might be just
enough to launch this troubled action flick

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:51.479
to a bit more success than predicted.

00:06:51.479 --> 00:06:55.909
Thanks for watching! Click the Looper icon
to subscribe to our YouTube channel. Plus

00:06:55.909 --> 00:06:58.599
check out all this cool stuff we know you'll
love, too!

